meta {
  name: 5. Unlink Driver from Torg
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/drivers/{{driverId}}/owner
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

docs {
  Inverse of steps 3/4 — releases the driver from their current torg. Restricted server-side to
  VAHN_ADMIN or the driver's currently-owning torg (a different torg admin gets 400, not just a
  coarse role rejection).

  Compensation details are reset, but the driver keeps their DRIVER role and DL verification —
  they can be re-linked (step 3 or 4) again afterwards without re-onboarding. Useful for
  resetting state between test runs.

  400 — "Driver is not linked to any torg", or "Not authorized to modify this driver" if the
  caller's torg doesn't own this driver. 404 — driver id doesn't exist.
}
